            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Malayalam for luck, then the Malayalam for as fate willed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: യുഗം",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "യുഗം — yugaṁ — \"an era; an age\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഇത് ഇന്റർനെറ്റിന്റെ യുഗമാണ്. itŭ inṟarneṟṟinṟe yugamāṇŭ. This is the age of the internet."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In old tales a യുഗം (yugaṁ) is one of the great ages of the world; today it is any era."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "യുഗം (yugaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit yuga, first \"a yoke, a pair\" (CDIAL 10482), and in later Sanskrit also an age of the world (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
