          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഭൂതകാലം — bhūtakālaṁ — \"the past\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "അവൻ ഭൂതകാലത്തെക്കുറിച്ച് ഒന്നും പറഞ്ഞില്ല. avan bhūtakālattekkuṟiccŭ onnuṁ paṟaññilla. He said nothing about the past."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In grammar, the past tense. ഭാവി, the future, is its opposite."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഭൂതകാലം (bhūtakālaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit bhūtakāla, \"past time; the past tense\" (Monier-Williams): bhūta, \"what has been\", and kāla, \"time\" (CDIAL 3084), the word that gave കാലം."
            }
          ]
        },
