            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സന്ദർഭം — sandarbhaṁ — \"an occasion; a context\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ആ സന്ദർഭത്തിൽ ഞാൻ ഒന്നും പറഞ്ഞില്ല. ā sandarbhattil ñān onnuṁ paṟaññilla. On that occasion I said nothing."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also the context of a word or a sentence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സന്ദർഭം (sandarbhaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit saṁdarbha, \"a stringing or weaving together; a composition\" (Monier-Williams). An occasion is how things are strung together at one time."
            }
          ]
